
⏺ The script is now parameterized. Here's the summary of changes:

  New command-line interface:
  # FreeBSD 15.0 with ZFS (OpenZFS 2.4 with O_DIRECT support)
  ./tigerbeetle-freebsd-complete-merged.sh --version=15.0-RELEASE --rootfs=zfs

  # FreeBSD 14.3 with UFS
  ./tigerbeetle-freebsd-complete-merged.sh --version=14.3-RELEASE --rootfs=ufs

  # With local image (you already downloaded on Mac)
  ./tigerbeetle-freebsd-complete-merged.sh --version=15.0-RELEASE --rootfs=zfs \
      --image=/path/to/FreeBSD-15.0-RELEASE-amd64-zfs.qcow2.xz

  Key changes:
  1. Required params: --version and --rootfs (explicit, no guessing)
  2. Optional: --image for local pre-downloaded images
  3. Version-aware URL patterns: 14.x uses no suffix, 15.x uses -ufs/-zfs
  4. Storage setup: Conditionally creates UFS filesystem or ZFS pool (tbpool) based on --rootfs
  5. Dynamic os-variant: Uses freebsd14.0 or freebsd15.0 for virt-install

  For your ZFS + O_DIRECT testing on FreeBSD 15.0:

  The ZFS setup creates:
  - Pool: tbpool (ashift=12, compression=lz4, atime=off)
  - Dataset: tbpool/tigerbeetle/data
  - Mount: /tbdata

  This gives you OpenZFS 2.4 with full O_DIRECT support for comparing AIO+kqueue vs io_uring.
